## 2. Data derived from bcv-commons - CC BY-SA 4.0

The Hebrew and Greek word lists in `config/cast-rules.toml`, and the example lyric sheets in
`examples/`, are built from bcv-commons datasets under CC BY-SA 4.0 (see [ATTRIBUTION.md](ATTRIBUTION.md)).
They are shared under the same licence, [CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).
Credit: bcv-commons; MACULA (Clear Bible / Biblica, CC BY 4.0).

What the tool generates (the cast table in `cache/`, the lyric sheets in `output/`, neither in this
repository) combines the public-domain BSB text with this structure, so it carries the same CC BY-SA 4.0
credit; each sheet's notes file holds it.

## 3. Vendored code - CC0

`vendor/verse_text/` is bcv-commons/bibles `tools/verse-text`, dedicated to the public domain (CC0 1.0);
see `vendor/verse_text/LICENSE-bibles`.

The Berean Standard Bible text itself is in the public domain (berean.bible). It is downloaded at run
time and not stored here.
